    "design_decisions": [
      {
        "decision": "Loader stays INSIDE index.html behind extraction markers; not split to a second file",
        "rejected_alternative": "renderer/catio.js loaded via classic <script src>",
        "reasoning": "renderer/README.md self-host path 1 is 'download index.html and open it'. A second file makes that path load successfully with bundle support silently absent — an L1 regression value #1 exists to prevent. The type=module CORS trap is a separate hazard the strategist flagged; a classic src avoids that one but not this one."
      },
      {
        "decision": "Client reads resp.arrayBuffer(), not resp.json()",
        "reasoning": "Content-sniffing then decides for both shapes, so the client half is compatible with the proxy as it behaves today AND after the passthrough fix. Decouples the two halves from a flag day."
      },
      {
        "decision": "Central directory is authoritative for sizes and methods; local-header size fields ignored",
        "reasoning": "Stream-written ZIPs may write zeros in the local header with real values in a trailing data descriptor. Trusting local headers returns empty members for exactly the archives an exporter is most likely to produce. Proven by negative control 1 and by ft-renderer-catio-06."
      },
      {
        "decision": "DecompressionStream constructed lazily, per deflated member",
        "reasoning": "A stored-only bundle then opens on engines with no deflate-raw support at all, which covers the adopter's photo shape on Chrome 80-102."
      },
      {
        "decision": "Fixtures generated at test time; 267 KB binary NOT committed",
        "reasoning": "Matches test_catio_bundle.py:22 convention. Real JPEG bytes add nothing to a SHA-256 byte-exactness assertion; they matter only for visual verification, which is a browser task. Generated set additionally covers a data-descriptor archive, which the supplied fixture could not."
      },
      {
        "decision": "rotation/caption/slot/is_primary implemented; crop_mode and deskew NOT",
        "reasoning": "Correct freeform crop needs real geometry and the canonical bundle uses crop_mode, so a bad implementation would render the reference catalog wrongly — worse than rendering it uncropped. Outside the MUST being fixed and outside the stated acceptance criteria. Wants its own item."
      }
